    "question": "James writes from 1 PM to 4 PM every night.  He can write 5 pages per hour.  How many weeks will it take to finish his 735-page book?",
    "gold": "7",
    "answer": "He writes for 4-1=<<4-1=3>>3 hours per day\nThat means he writes 3*5=<<3*5=15>>15 pages per day\nSo it would take him 735/15=<<735/15=49>>49 days\nThat means it will take 49/7=<<49/7=7>>7 weeks\n#### 7"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many weeks it will take James to finish his 735-page book, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of hours James writes each night.\n2. Determine how many pages James writes each night.\n3. Calculate the total number of pages James writes in one week.\n4. Determine how many weeks it will take to write 735 pages.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of hours James writes each night:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ PM} - 1 \\text{ PM} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, we determine how many pages James writes each night:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ hours} \\times 5 \\text{ pages per hour} = 15 \\text{ pages per night} \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the total number of pages James writes in one week:\n\\[ 15 \\text{ pages per night} \\times 7 \\text{ days per week} = 105 \\text{ pages per week} \\]\n\nFinally, we determine how many weeks it will take to write 735 pages:\n\\[ \\frac{735 \\text{ pages}}{105 \\text{ pages per week}} = 7 \\text{ weeks} \\]\n\nThus, it will take James \\(\\boxed{7}\\) weeks to finish his 735-page book.",
